    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is anchored by **Tyler Soderstrom**, whose 76.91 efficiency score makes him our premier start. He benefits immensely from a plus-matchup against McGreevy, pairing favorable park factors with a move into the #3 hole in the order. Joining him in the top tier is **Brice Turang**, who checks in at 63.20. **Brice Turang** earns his status as a lock today thanks to his favorable placement at the top of the lineup and a solid matchup against Canning; he remains the primary engine for our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases and run production. **Josh Naylor** also clears the 60-point threshold, thriving in the heart of the order where he remains a high-floor play despite a respectable opponent in Burrows.\n\nWe were forced to be disciplined on the bench, where **Cole Young** ultimately fell just short of a starting berth with a 39.51 score. While his base metrics are respectable, his status in the #9 slot and a dip in park factors kept him under our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" We are monitoring the situation for **Trevor Story** and **Seiya Suzuki** closely; both are facing elite arms in Luzardo and Sale respectively, suppressing their scores to the 45-47 range. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** shows a strong 57.00, his platoon disadvantage against Kay is significant, necessitating a cautious outlook. We are prioritizing the upside of **James Wood** in the leadoff spot\u2014whose favorable wind conditions and strong xwOBA help mitigate the threat of Burns\u2014over the fringe bench bats like **Mickey Moniak** and **Zach McKinstry**, both of whom remain sidelined to preserve our strict game caps while they face difficult starting rotations.",
